1
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:11,280
Hello, in this section as part of our discussion on research activities and especially a part

2
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:16,520
of discussion on experimental research activities, we will look at safety in our research lab

3
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,520
setting.

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:22,320
So, now safety is something that is a very broad subject, it is a subject that is dealt

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:29,400
with in great detail in many occupational working condition kind of situations.

6
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,960
And so, what we are going to do here is briefly just highlight specific aspects of

7
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:38,600
safety associated with some of the common things that people encounter in their labs.

8
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:43,080
If you want a much more elaborate discussion on safety, you really have to attend courses

9
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:47,800
which are focused on safety and some of the points that I am highlighting in this very

10
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:52,980
brief section here are actually points that are elaborated upon in great detail in many

11
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:58,760
of the safety courses that are there, many of them are there internationally and you

12
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:03,640
should certainly I mean take a course to actually looking at those courses to fully

13
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:08,440
understand the range of concerns that exist with respect to safety.

14
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:12,960
Now, safety is there in industrial setting, it is also there in research lab setting,

15
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:16,360
there is one major difference I feel that exists between an industrial setting and

16
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,840
research lab setting.

17
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:22,800
In the industrial setting, the typically the activities that each person carries out

18
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:27,400
in the industry is actually well defined and so, there is very little variability in

19
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,360
that activity, little variation in that activity over a period of time.

20
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:38,480
Therefore, the procedures that they follow, the safety equipment that they have and the

21
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:43,040
aspects of safety that they focus on are actually well defined for each individual.

22
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:47,240
In a research lab setting actually quite the opposite is true, most of the time we

23
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:51,680
are trying to do new experiments, we are making new experimental setups and we are

24
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,080
trying out some new feature in our experiment and so on.

25
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,520
And therefore, we are often pushing the boundaries in various different directions

26
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:03,280
and so, we have to be even more actively involved in figuring out the aspects of

27
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:07,640
that experiment that require us to be more careful and you know where we have to

28
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:12,040
put in more effort and ensure that there is that the experiment is carried out

29
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,040
safely.

30
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:16,320
Now, safety is important for all the people who are present in the lab, for

31
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:20,760
yourself for and also for the equipment and even for the experiment itself.

32
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:25,480
Now, I would also like to point out that you know safety is an aspect of culture.

33
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:28,840
So, it is something that you have to build into you, it does not happen overnight,

34
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:32,560
it is not something that you know it is just not just a matter of following just

35
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:36,920
a few procedures, it is being involved in the process of safety and only then you

36
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:40,280
can actually you know make your workplace a very safe workplace.

37
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:45,080
Now, in a typical lab some of the things that you would see in a typical lab which

38
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:49,160
require you know formal ways of you know addressing so that you do it in a safe

39
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:53,480
manner are first of all in most labs you would see chemicals, so chemicals is

40
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:57,360
something that is very common in most labs you will have you know acids, you

41
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:02,360
are going to have bases, you are going to have maybe powder samples, maybe

42
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,240
